{"step_index":111,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:17:59Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T10:17:59Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T10:17:59Z\nShowing lines 1-67 of 67\n1: # Host log review — 2026-10-24\n2: \n3: Task: `host-log-review-20261024`. Agent: Codex `/root`, local caller `jeremy` (UID 1000), with authorized read-only host diagnostics through `sudo -n`.\n4: \n5: Observed approximately 18:01–18:05 UTC / 14:01–14:05 EDT. Host `3tched`; boot ID `6767d86f-0030-439f-8471-dc078144167a`; kernel `6.18.57-x64v3-op-release-lifetime1-xanmod1`. Repository HEAD: `86f03d2dede738e2d780ab789dd5800b58678479`. The checkout already contained extensive unrelated modifications; this task adds only this report.\n6: \n7: ## Outcome\n8: \n9: The host is running after its approximately 17:58 UTC reboot, with ample current memory and disk headroom. There was a significant OOM incident earlier today, and several application, desktop, and logging faults remain. No repair, service restart, build, test suite, deployment, grant change, or storage mutation was performed.\n10: \n11: Live `/etc/os-release` identifies **Devuan GNU/Linux 6 (excalibur)**, despite the supplied repository guidance describing Artix. PID 1 is **runit** and live service links resolve into `/etc/sv` or packaged runit definitions. This is a verified environment discrepancy, not authorization to change the operating system or repository policy.\n12: \n13: ## Coverage and evidence\n14: \n15: - Inventoried 1,417 files under `/var/log`. Searched retained text logs, including supported compressed rotations, for warning/error/failure patterns and separately for OOM, crashes, filesystem errors, and lockups. The broad pattern scan found matches in 592 files; those counts include historical messages, duplication, and harmless keyword matches and are not incident counts. Scan stderr was empty.\n16: - Inspected current runit/application logs, system/kernel/authentication/boot logs, Incus